    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "a woollen fabric 30 yards in length, originally made in a parish in Norfolk, north of Norwich (OEngl Wurdestede, later Wurthstede, Worthsted), made from well-twisted yarn spun of long-staple wool combed to lay the fibers parallel; single, half-double and double refer to the thickness of the cloth (OED s.v. worsted); also manufactured in St Omer (imported)" ;
